## 6. Test seed support

### Java — `/home/daniel/ui-sandbox/src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/TestSupportController.java`
Full contents already shown in the tool output above. Key points for invoice notes:
- `/__test__/reset` truncates `notes` (via `TRUNCATE TABLE notes RESTART IDENTITY`) along with all other domain tables; it drops referential integrity first.
- `/__test__/seed` handles a `notes` fixture array (lines 224-247). Each note takes `id`, `targetType`, `targetId`, `text`, and optional `at` (ISO OffsetDateTime; defaults to now). After seeding it bumps the identity sequence past the max seeded id so API-created notes get fresh ids.
- **This already supports `targetType: 'invoice'`** — the seed is fully generic. The relevant note-seeding block:
```java
List<Map<String, Object>> notes =
        (List<Map<String, Object>>) fixture.getOrDefault("notes", List.of());
long maxNoteId = 0;
for (Map<String, Object> n : notes) {
    java.time.OffsetDateTime at = n.get("at") != null
            ? java.time.OffsetDateTime.parse(n.get("at").toString())
            : java.time.OffsetDateTime.now();
    long noteId = ((Number) n.get("id")).longValue();
    jdbc.update(
            "INSERT INTO notes (id, target_type, target_id, text, created_at)"
                    + " VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?)",
            noteId, n.get("targetType"), ((Number) n.get("targetId")).longValue(),
            n.get("text"), at);
    maxNoteId = Math.max(maxNoteId, noteId);
}
if (maxNoteId > 0) {
    jdbc.execute("ALTER TABLE notes ALTER COLUMN id RESTART WITH " + (maxNoteId + 1));
}
```
So a spec seeds invoice notes with e.g. `notes: [{ id: 1, targetType: 'invoice', targetId: 1, text: '...', at: '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z' }]`.

### Frontend — `/home/daniel/ui-sandbox/e2e/support/seed.ts`
